// EightMax 5.2: decision study runner (mwcli --study, POST /api/study/start).
//
// A study fixture ("EightMax study fixture", formatVersion 1) describes one poker decision: the game as the
// application builds it (variants[].nativeSpec, generated by the normal Multiway workflow), the decision
// (action path, board cards on the path, hero seat and hand) and a study plan (seeds, sampled-deal budgets,
// trainer, evaluator settings and a DECLARED tolerance). For every variant and seed the runner trains a fresh
// engine through the budgets and, after each budget, asks the existing evaluators for
//   - the hero hand's average-strategy frequency and action EVs at the decision (mw_action_ev; exact where the
//     fixture says so, otherwise sampled with common random numbers: every sample evaluates all actions on the
//     same cards and continuation draws, so EV differences are paired),
//   - the quality of the surrounding strategy (mw_response_gain; exact best-response gains inside the
//     abstraction, or sampled one-shot deviations, which are a lower bound and cannot certify an equilibrium).
// Two sources of uncertainty are kept apart in the result:
//   evaluation sampling   the standard error of one evaluation of one trained strategy (zero for exact)
//   trained strategies    the spread of the same quantity across independently seeded trainings
// Nothing here changes training: the engines are driven through the public mw_* interface only.
